@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Theme resolution on load
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
participant "Browser" as browser
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "Global stylesheet" as global
  participant "tokens.scss" as tokens
  participant "Component stylesheets" as css
end box
user -> browser : Open the app with the OS set to light or dark
browser -> global : Load the global stylesheet before first paint
global -> tokens : Include the light and dark token sets
browser -> browser : Evaluate prefers-color-scheme
alt OS is set to dark
  tokens --> browser : Dark token set applies (L2-026)
else OS is set to light
  tokens --> browser : Light token set applies (L2-026)
end
browser -> css : Resolve every colour through a custom property (L2-026)
css --> browser : Computed colours for the active theme
browser --> user : First paint in the matching theme, no flash of the other theme (L2-026)
note over browser, tokens
  No script selects the theme and no manual toggle exists in v1 (L2-026)
end note
opt OS appearance changes while the app is open
  browser -> browser : Re-evaluate prefers-color-scheme
  browser --> user : Repaint with the other token set (L2-026)
end
@enduml
